* December 7th - '''AaB esport''' release their roster. <ref name="roster disbanded 2021"> {{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1468128151326834697|date=2021-12-07|title=OPDATERING! Vi siger farvel til holdet|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=UPDATE! We say goodbye to the team|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>

|content6=<!--2024-->
* August 31st - '''AaB esport''' announce their lineup, consisting of [[PihLziNh0]], [[m0vski-]], [[N4XX1$]], [[Knuten]], [[SaMsInG]], [[Poseidon (Danish player)|Poseidon]] as coach, [[Django]] as analyst, and [[money]] as team manager. <ref name="aab roster 2024">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1829930009722535954|title=Nogle af jer har måske allerede gættet det! Men vi er stadig glade for at kunne annoncere AaB's nye lineup i Powerligaen og ESEA|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=Some of you may have already guessed it But we are still excited to announce AaB's new lineup in Powerligaen and ESEA|date=2024-08-31|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* October 21st - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[Poseidon (Danish player)|Poseidon]]. <ref name="-Poseidon">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1848319255978049755|title=@ThePoseidonCS træder tilbage som træner for vores main hold for at fokusere på sin egen spilkarriere|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=@ThePoseidonCS steps down as coach for our main team to focus on his own gaming career|date=2024-10-21|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* November 15th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[PihLziNh0]]. <ref name="-PihLziNh0">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1857415653734383799|title=Det er ofte svært at sige farvel – især til en person, der har været afgørende for, at dette projekt overhovedet blev en realitet|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=It is often difficult to say goodbye – especially to a person who has been crucial in making this project a reality at all|date=2024-11-15|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* November 26th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[Django]] and [[Knuten]]. <ref name="-Django -Knuten">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1861475419922538889|title=Vi har truffet nogle svære beslutninger i dag|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=We have made some tough decisions today|date=2024-11-26|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* December 10th - '''AaB esport''' sign [[b0ychild]] as coach. <ref name="+b0ychild">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1866507223381180755|title=Vi er begejstrede for at præsentere AaB's nye træner|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=We are excited to present AaB's new coach|date=2024-12-10|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* December 12th - '''AaB esport''' sign [[Fröhlich]]. <ref name="+Fröhlich">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1867160342691983749|title=Der er spændende nyt fra AaB's 1. divisionshold!|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=There's exciting news from AaB's 1st division team!|date=2024-12-12|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* December 16th - '''AaB esport''' sign [[fa1th]]. <ref name="+fa1th">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1868686245771284681|title=Lineupen for det nye år er klar, og vi er stolte af at præsentere @fa1thof!|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=The lineup for the new year is ready, and we are proud to present @fa1thof!|date=2024-12-16|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>

|content7=<!--2025-->
* January 1st - [[b0ychild]] is acquired by [[XI Esport]]. <ref name="-b0ychild">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/XIESPORTGG/status/1874398776422785276|title=We’re proud to announce the new lineup representing XI Esport|date=2025-01-01|author=[[XI Esport]]}}</ref>
* May 2nd - '''AaB esport''' sign [[Macho]] as their new coach. <ref name="+Macho">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1918371814788800772|title=Vi har i noget tid været på udkig efter den rette træner til AaB Main, og vi er glade for endelig at kunne sige, at jagten er slut|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=We have been looking for the right coach for AaB Main for some time, and we are thrilled to finally be able to say that the search is over|date=2025-05-02|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* June 16th - '''AaB esport''' release their roster. <ref name="roster disbanded 2025"> {{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1934624901412859936|title=AaB Esport søger nye spillere til vores nuværende main lineup|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=AaB Esport is looking for new players for our current main lineup|date=2025-06-16|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* July 8th - '''AaB esport''' announce their new lineup consisting of [[Viggo]], [[Boye]], [[qx]], [[SinK]], and [[Tubsy]] as coach. Additionally, they add [[stesso]] on a trial basis. <ref name="aab roster 2025">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1942533646461673927|title=The moment you've all been waiting for – it's time for the big announcement!|date=2025-07-08|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* July 20th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[Tubsy]]. <ref name="-Tubsy"> {{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/1968944626498252856|title=Thank you @Tubsy1337 for your help building up our team - Actually, and to be fair, you haven't been with us since EPIC lan, so we might have to call you in again soon cause the results haven't been as we wanted...But thank you for Coaching us and helping us|date=2025-09-19|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* August 1st - [[stesso]] completes his trial successfully and joins the team on a permanent basis. <ref name="stesso trial">{{inside source|source=MgHz|date=2025-09-19}}</ref>
* October 16th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[SinK]]. <ref name="bench SinK">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/1978820576560001414|title=Roster update|date=2025-10-16|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* October 17th - '''AaB esport''' sign [[BehinDx]] as [[Boye]] is acquired by an undisclosed organization, later revealed to be [[Tricked Esport]]. <ref name="+behindx">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/1979087009390956605|title=Transfer news|date=2025-10-17|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref><ref name="-boye">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/aabesportelite/status/1979270154560376921?s=46&t=zGZ3hfeIdQqWk5L_TC14Nw|title=Transfer news|date=2025-10-17|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* October 18th - '''AaB esport''' acquire [[Queenix]] from [[Tricked Esport]]. <ref name="+Queenix">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/1979426627625873814|title=Queenix joins AaB Esport!|date=2025-10-18|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* November 12th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[BehinDx]]. <ref name="-behindx">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/BehinDxcs/status/1988580811856367651|title=LFT - Looking for team|date=2025-11-12|author=[[BehinDx]]}}</ref>
* November 21st - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[Queenix]], sign [[bekker]], and acquire [[Mol011]] from [[Prestige Esport]]. <ref name="-Queenix">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/1991849188733108505|title=Roster change|date=2025-11-21|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref><ref name="+bekker +Mol011">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/1991969433338761342|title=Big News from AaB Esport!|date=2025-11-21|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* November 25th - '''AaB esport''' sign [[Gnøffe]] as coach. <ref name="+Gnøffe">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/1993441729723121789|title=Roster update|date=2025-11-25|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* December 25th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[Viggo]], [[stesso]], and [[Gnøffe]]. <ref name="-viggo -stesso">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/2004184338489860602|title=Roster changes heading into 2026|date=2025-12-25|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* December 26th - '''AaB esport''' acquire [[N4XX1$]] from [[Vendetta Gaming]]. <ref name="+n4xx1$">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/2004516672296648852|title=Transfer completed|date=2025-12-26|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>

|content8=<!--2026-->
* January 1st - '''AaB esport''' acquire [[Maze]] from [[BIG Academy]]. <ref name="+maze">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/2006753276063068282|title=Finally, we are proud to announce our latest signing, who will be joining our active roster for 2026|date=2026-01-01|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* January 24th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[N4XX1$]]. <ref name="-n4xx1$">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/N4XX1S/status/2015106299697000751|title=Sadly my stay at @AaBesport has come to an end|date=2026-01-24|author=[[N4XX1$]]}}</ref>
* February 1st - '''AaB esport''' part ways with [[Mol011]] and acquire [[n1Xen]] and [[sSen]] from [[Copenhagen Wolves (American organization)|Copenhagen Wolves]] and [[Wildcard]], respectively. <ref name="+n1Xen +sSen">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/2017992462401171517|title=From November–December ’25, we set out to figure out what our roster should look like, and throughout that entire build, our ranking has only moved in one direction: up|date=2026-02-01|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* April 11th - '''AaB esport''' bench [[qx]] and acquire [[anber]] from [[ALGO Esports]]. <ref name="+anber">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/2043056321289953503|title=Change of active roster|date=2026-04-11|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* May 5th - [[qx]] is acquired by [[Prestige Esport]]. <ref name="-qx">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/Aabesportelite/status/2051686015127920951|title=TRANSFER NEWS|date=2026-05-05|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* May 14th - '''AaB esport''' part ways with their ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' division as they go on and form [[Esport Academy Copenhagen]]. <ref name="eac">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/2054816645084807523|title=AaB esport stopper CS eliteinvolveringen|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=AaB esport stops CS elite involvement|date=2026-05-14|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* July 31st - '''AaB esport''' promote their [[AaB Bulls]] roster consisting of [[Few]], [[Beddy]], [[Bukhavez]], [[noike]], and [[Djdamecykel]] to serve as their main squad. <ref name="bulls promoted">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/AaBesport/status/2083211688195620971|title=AaB Bulls bliver ny main lineup|language={{Flag|dk}} Danish|trans_title=AaB Bulls becomes new main lineup|date=2026-07-31|author='''AaB esport'''}}</ref>
* September 28th - [[Bukhavez]] is acquired by [[MASONIC]]. <ref name="-bukhavez">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/MasonicGG/status/2104529047489478708|title=ROSTER UPDATE|date=2026-09-28|author=[[MASONIC]]}}</ref>
}}

